                    <div class="col-md-12">

                        <div class="shadow-lg p-3 mb-3 bg-body rounded" style="padding-left:2%;max-width:100%">


                            <h5 style="color:orange">Course Highlights</h5>
                            <div class="mb-3 mt-2">
                                A professional Python programming course typically bridges the gap between basic syntax and industry-ready application. Key highlights often include a mix of core fundamentals, advanced concepts, and specialized libraries for high-growth fields like Data Science and AI.
                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3 mt-2">

                                <ul>

                                    <li>

                                        <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>
                                        <b>Syntax & Logic</b>:
                                        <div class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Mastery of variables, data types (strings, integers, booleans), and control flow (if-else statements, for/while loops).
                                        </div>

                                    </li>

                                   
                                    <li>
                                        <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>
                                        <b>Data Collections</b>:
                                        <div class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            In-depth training on Python’s built-in structures: Lists, Tuples, Sets, and Dictionaries.
                                        </div>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>
                                        <b>Functions & Modules</b>:
                                        <div class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Learning to write reusable code using functions, passing arguments (*args, **kwargs), and organizing code into modules.
                                        </div>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>
                                        <b>Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)</b>:
                                        <div class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Designing scalable systems using Classes, Objects, Inheritance, and Polymorphism
                                        </div>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>
                                        <b>File Handling & Data Streams</b>:
                                        <div class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Reading/writing various file formats (Text, CSV, JSON) and managing directories.
                                        </div>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>
                                        <b>Exception Handling</b>:
                                        <div class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Using try, except, and finally blocks to create robust, error-resistant applications.
                                        </div>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <i class="bi-star-fill" style="color:orange"></i>
                                        <b>Database Interaction</b>:
                                        <div class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Connecting Python to SQL databases (MySQL, SQLite) for CRUD operations.
                                        </div>
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>



                        <div class="shadow-lg p-3 mb-3 bg-body rounded" style="padding-left:2%;margin-top:2% ;max-width:100%">

                            <h5 style="color:orange">
                                Who can do?
                            </h5>
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                A Data Structures and Algorithms (DSA) course is suitable for anyone interested in software engineering, regardless of their current background. While traditionally associated with Computer Science majors, the modern tech landscape has made it accessible and often essential for a broad range of learners in 2026.
                            </div>
                            <div class="mb-3">
                                <ul>
                                    <li>
                                        <b>Students</b> :
                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Graduates, postgraduates, and even 10th or 12th-grade students can take these courses. While some formal degrees (like B.E. or B.Sc.) may be preferred for advanced career tracks, they are not mandatory for basic training.
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <b>Career Switchers </b> :
                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Professionals from non-IT backgrounds (marketing, finance, etc.) who want to transition into tech roles or automate their current workflows.
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <b>Working Professionals</b> :
                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Existing developers, system analysts, or managers looking to upskill for modern projects in AI, data science, or automation.
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                    <li>
                                        <b>Beginners with Zero Experience</b> :
                                        <p class="mb-3" style="margin-left:2%">
                                            Most introductory courses assume no prior coding knowledge and teach fundamentals from scratch.
                                        </p>
                                    </li>
                                </ul>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
